#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:286
msgid "*high*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:31
msgid ""
"The CPU frequency scaling subsystem ensures that the processor can operate "
"at its maximum supported frequency.  While, in general, bootloaders are "
"tasked with setting the CPU clock to the highest speed on boot, some do "
"not.  It is thus desirable to keep this option enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:38
msgid ""
"A real-time kernel is not about being \"as fast as possible\", however real-"
"time requirements may demand that the CPU is clocked at a particular speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:43
msgid "``CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_PERFORMANCE``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:48
msgid ""
"Real-Time workloads expect a fixed CPU frequency during execution.  Using "
"the performance governor is an easy way to achieve that purely from kernel "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:52
msgid ""
"This is not an absolute rule.  Some setups might prefer to clock the CPU to "
"lower speeds due to thermal packaging or other requirements.  The key is "
"that the CPU frequency remains constant once set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:57
msgid "Non-performance CPU frequency governors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:59
#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:114
#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:167
#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:213
#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:270
#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:285
msgid "disabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:60
#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:141
#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:168
msgid "*medium*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:62
msgid ""
"To ensure reproducible system latency measurements, disable the non-"
"``PERFORMANCE`` CPU frequency governors whenever possible.  This avoids the "
"risk of unknown userspace tasks implicitly or explicitly setting a different "
"CPU frequency governor, and thereby changing latency behavior while the "
"system is running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:68
msgid ""
"If disabling other frequency governors is not an option, use a governor that "
"keeps the CPU frequency fixed.  For example, "
"``CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_USERSPACE`` can be enabled when userspace is "
"responsible for setting a *stable* frequency during system initialization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:73
msgid ""
"If a low CPU frequency is desired, then "
"``CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_POWERSAVE`` can be set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:76
msgid ""
"The ``ONDEMAND`` governor should not be enabled on a real-time system.  Its "
"frequency changes depend on workload behavior and can significantly harm "
"determinism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:80
msgid "For more information, see Documentation/admin-guide/pm/cpufreq.rst"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:83
msgid "``CONFIG_CPU_IDLE``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:86
#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:115
#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:197
msgid "*info*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:88
msgid ""
"CPU idle states (C-states) allow the processor to enter low-power modes "
"during periods of inactivity.  Very-low CPU idle states may require flushing "
"the CPU caches and lowering or disabling the clocking.  This can lower power "
"consumption, but it also increases the entry and exit latency from such "
"states."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:94
msgid ""
"While disabling this option eliminates cpuidle-related latencies, doing so "
"can significantly impact hardware longevity, warranty, and thermal behavior. "
"Users should cap the maximum C-state to C1 instead.  For ACPI platforms, "
"this can be achieved by using the boot parameter [1]_::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:101
msgid ""
"Higher C-states can be acceptable depending on the user workload's latency "
"requirements.  For ACPI-based platforms, use the ``cpupower idle-info`` "
"command to inspect the available idle states."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/real-time/kernel-configuration.rst:105
msgid "For more information, please see:"
